  "id": "psychopathy",
  "term": "psychopathy",
  "definition": "Psychopathy is a pattern of social difficulty that interferes with functioning in society. In this source, it is described as having two broad dimensions—interpersonal-affective and lifestyle-antisocial—which are linked to different trait patterns and differences in how emotional faces, especially negative expressions, are processed.",
